    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b38f74d2-6e06-448f-96e9-2ef682d8aff3"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n## Scatter plots\nJokes aside, the idea is to use them \
to plot data points, ideally with error bars. We can't simply put our \
squircles as `PlotMarker`, since it is very inefficient and will eventually \
crash on over 1000 data points.\n\nFor this reason, we use the power of \
JavaScript and the simplest superellipse approach. I will leave out the \
details of implementation, since this is a plain frontend symbol with a \
generated path using a bunch of SVG magic:", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "1f9cb318-958b-4fb6-a08c-36b8ee76667c", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b38f74d2-6e06-448f-96e9-2ef682d8aff3"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "## Scatter plots\nJokes aside, the idea is to use them to \
plot data points, ideally with error bars. We can't simply put our squircles \
as `PlotMarker`, since it is very inefficient and will eventually crash on \
over 1000 data points.\n\nFor this reason, we use the power of JavaScript and \
the simplest superellipse approach. I will leave out the details of \
implementation, since this is a plain frontend symbol with a generated path \
using a bunch of SVG magic:", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "6da407f9-83a5-4f76-86b9-b07c069f1fe6", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b38f74d2-6e06-448f-96e9-2ef682d8aff3"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".js\nfunction normalizePoints(data) {\n  if \
(!Array.isArray(data)) return [];\n  if (data.length === 0) return [];\n  if \
(!Array.isArray(data[0])) return [data];\n  return data;\n}\n\nfunction \
squirclePath(cx, cy, size, n = 4, steps = 32) {\n  const a = size / 2;\n  \
const b = size / 2;\n  const pts = [];\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) \
{\n    const t = (i / steps) * Math.PI * 2;\n    const ct = Math.cos(t);\n    \
const st = Math.sin(t);\n\n    const px = cx + a * Math.sign(ct) * \
Math.pow(Math.abs(ct), 2 / n);\n    const py = cy + b * Math.sign(st) * \
Math.pow(Math.abs(st), 2 / n);\n\n    pts.push([px, py]);\n  }\n\n  return \
pts.length\n    ? `M ${pts[0][0]} ${pts[0][1]} ` +\n        \
pts.slice(1).map(p => `L ${p[0]} ${p[1]}`).join(\" \") +\n        \" Z\"\n    \
: \"\";\n}\n\ncore.Squircle = async (args, env) => {\n  let data = await \
interpretate(args[0], env);\n  if (data instanceof NumericArrayObject) {\n    \
data = data.normal();\n  }\n\n  const x = env.xAxis;\n  const y = \
env.yAxis;\n\n  data = normalizePoints(data);\n\n  const size = env.pointSize \
* 200;\n  const exponent = 4;\n  const steps = 32;\n\n  const object = \
env.svg.append(\"g\")\n    .style(\"opacity\", env.opacity);\n\n  \
data.forEach((d) => {\n    const cx = x(d[0]);\n    const cy = y(d[1]);\n\n   \
 object.append(\"path\")\n      .attr(\"d\", squirclePath(cx, cy, size, \
exponent, steps))\n      .style(\"fill\", env.color);\n  });\n\n  return \
object;\n};\n\ncore.SquircleErr = async (args, env) => {\n  let data = await \
interpretate(args[0], env);\n  if (data instanceof NumericArrayObject) {\n    \
data = data.normal();\n  }\n\n  const x = env.xAxis;\n  const y = \
env.yAxis;\n\n  data = normalizePoints(data);\n\n  const size = env.pointSize \
* 200;\n  const exponent = 4;\n  const steps = 32;\n\n  const object = \
env.svg.append(\"g\")\n    .style(\"opacity\", env.opacity);\n\n  \
data.forEach((d) => {\n    const cx = x(d[0]);\n    const cy = y(d[1]);\n    \
const err = d[2];\n\n    if (typeof err === \"number\" && \
Number.isFinite(err)) {\n      const y1 = y(d[1] - err);\n      const y2 = \
y(d[1] + err);\n      const capWidth = Math.max(6, size * 0.35);\n\n      \
object.append(\"line\")\n        .attr(\"x1\", cx)\n        .attr(\"y1\", \
y1)\n        .attr(\"x2\", cx)\n        .attr(\"y2\", y2)\n        \
.style(\"stroke\", env.color)\n        .style(\"stroke-width\", 1.5)\n        \
.style(\"fill\", \"none\");\n\n      object.append(\"line\")\n        \
.attr(\"x1\", cx - capWidth / 2)\n        .attr(\"y1\", y1)\n        \
.attr(\"x2\", cx + capWidth / 2)\n        .attr(\"y2\", y1)\n        \
.style(\"stroke\", env.color)\n        .style(\"stroke-width\", 1.5)\n        \
.style(\"fill\", \"none\");\n\n      object.append(\"line\")\n        \
.attr(\"x1\", cx - capWidth / 2)\n        .attr(\"y1\", y2)\n        \
.attr(\"x2\", cx + capWidth / 2)\n        .attr(\"y2\", y2)\n        \
.style(\"stroke\", env.color)\n        .style(\"stroke-width\", 1.5)\n        \
.style(\"fill\", \"none\");\n    }\n\n    object.append(\"path\")\n      \
.attr(\"d\", squirclePath(cx, cy, size, exponent, steps))\n      \
.style(\"fill\", env.color);\n  });\n\n  return object;\n};", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
